# Control height and toolbars

`--control-h` is **44px** in `admin/src/index.css`. These selectors already set `height` and `min-height` to that token:

- `[data-slot='button']` (not icon sizes, not `link`)
- `[data-slot='input']`, `[data-slot='select-trigger']`, `[data-slot='input-group']`

Do not give a new single-line button, input, or select its own height. Icon buttons inside the workspace stay square at `--control-h`. Textareas and link buttons are the exceptions.

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
button { height: 32px; }

/* ✅ GOOD — leave the data-slot rules in index.css in place */
```

Toolbars use `Toolbar` in `admin/src/components/toolbar.tsx`: a wrapping row, search and filters in flow, actions with `sm:ml-auto`. Below `sm`, search, each filter, and the action group are full width. Do not push actions with a flex spacer; it collapses on wrap.
